      "side": 1,
      "message": "This applies to the existing implementation, before aosp/3590992? After aosp/3590992, Linux IOMMU driver is not supposed to issue any invalidation requests before pKVM initialization, right? It seems that after aosp/3590992 we can just remove the below quiesce logic altogether?\n\nOn the other hand, AFAIK this issue was discovered precisely as a result of aosp/3590992 which triggered the issue on PTL, but on ADL for some reason there was no problem observed, i.e. there was some invalidation in flight despite the fact Linux IOMMU driver initialization is delayed until pKVM initialization? So, do we understand what is actually going on, i.e. who is issuing that early invalidation request on ADL even with aosp/3590992?",
      "range": {
