      "writtenOn": "2025-08-18T16:47:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This issue was seen after aosp/3590992. The very initial invalidation requests are from Interrupt remapping and I believe this is a timing issue that was uncovered when we delayed the iommu initialization. On fatcat, with the iommu init delay, we reach this code earlier and interrupt remapping wouldn\u0027t have got a chance to issue the invalidation. The theory is that - interrupt remapping on ADL might be quicker to issue the invalidation so that we don\u0027t see this issue. Verification of this theory is a TODO, will get to that soon :-).",
      "parentUuid": "2fbfdfe8_b3236b59",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1294,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 1295,
        "endChar": 65
      },
